      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `Years.ZERO` survives a serialization round-trip as the same singleton instance. I'll improve understandability by removing unused imports, removing the unrelated `data_invalid` method, and making the intent of each step clearer.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and the unrelated `data_invalid` helper, adds a comment explaining the singleton/`readResolve` contract being tested, and uses descriptive variable names (`originalSingleton`, `buffer`, `serializer`, `deserializer`, `deserializedInstance`) to make each step of the serialization round-trip self-explanatory."
